WEBVTT

00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:08.208
"Excel Saga"

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:11.792
You know, we were in a hurry.
Why weren't there any fries?

00:00:11.792 --> 00:00:13.958
And when I said I didn't
want the value meal,

00:00:13.958 --> 00:00:16.625
they treated them like separate
items and it got more expensive.

00:00:16.625 --> 00:00:20.000
I didn't really get that, but oh well.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.458
But I can't believe we've
actually made nineteen episodes.

00:00:23.458 --> 00:00:27.542
We're starting to run out of ideas
and falling behind in production,

00:00:27.542 --> 00:00:29.500
so what are we going to
do about the twentieth one?

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.125
Don't worry. I've got it covered.

00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:34.542
And I cooked something
up over here too.

00:00:34.542 --> 00:00:36.375
But I'm the one who wrote it.

00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:37.500
Ready, set...

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.750
"I, Koshi Rikdo,
hereby give permission

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.583
to summarize the Excel Saga anime."

00:00:43.792 --> 00:00:44.417
"Koshi Rikdo"

00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:46.292
I didn't approve that!

00:00:46.292 --> 00:00:47.333
Oops, sorry.

00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:48.792
All right, let's go drinking!

00:00:48.792 --> 00:00:49.875
I'm gonna drink till I puke!

00:00:49.875 --> 00:00:50.417
--I'm gonna puke till I drink!

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:52.167
--That wasn't the deal!
--I'm gonna puke till I drink!

00:01:02.625 --> 00:01:06.500
<i>Sore wa ai ja nai</i>

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.458
<i>Ai wa sore ja nai</i>

00:01:10.458 --> 00:01:18.333
<i>Aishite iru kedo aisarete wa inai</i>

00:01:18.333 --> 00:01:22.208
<i>Kesshite ai ja nai</i>

00:01:22.208 --> 00:01:26.292
<i>Ketsu wa ai ja nai</i>

00:01:26.292 --> 00:01:34.000
<i>Aisaretai keredo motometari wa shinai</i>

00:01:34.833 --> 00:01:38.708
<i>Kono mi sasagete inochi nagedashi</i>

00:01:38.708 --> 00:01:42.750
<i>Wakime mo furazu tada hitasura ni</i>

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:46.667
<i>Damashite sukashite yokohairi</i>

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:49.875
<i>Tanin o fumitaoshi keri o kamashite</i>

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:52.083
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>
<i>(Tonzura koite!)</i>

00:01:52.083 --> 00:01:54.000
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>
<i>(Tonzura koite!)</i>

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.875
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>
<i>(Tonzura koite!)</i>

00:01:55.875 --> 00:01:57.792
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>

00:01:57.792 --> 00:02:02.625
<i>Banana no kawa de korondemo</i>

00:02:02.625 --> 00:02:05.750
<i>Sore wa subete ano kata no tame</i>

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.375
<i>Shiite iu nara sore wa kitto</i>

00:02:10.375 --> 00:02:18.208
<i>Ai to iu na no chuuseishin</i>

00:02:24.625 --> 00:02:26.292
"Puke Bar"

00:02:26.292 --> 00:02:28.500
That's super-tasty!

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.000
Yo, electric chair! Excel here!

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.833
Lately, I feel like I haven't
had that many appearances.

00:02:33.833 --> 00:02:35.625
Is that because of my
ego as the main character?

00:02:35.625 --> 00:02:38.042
Or is it the intentional, lawful
conspiracy of the production side?

00:02:38.042 --> 00:02:40.208
Due to the haphazard
way the stories are created,

00:02:40.208 --> 00:02:43.292
you may sorta kinda feel that
abuse is cropping up everywhere,

00:02:43.292 --> 00:02:44.958
making for unbelievable developments.

00:02:44.958 --> 00:02:47.625
But I don't wanna get hurt
by a straightforward answer

00:02:47.625 --> 00:02:50.333
and they want me to stop,
so I've recently stopped asking.

00:02:50.333 --> 00:02:52.917
Perhaps they just ran out of ideas.

00:02:59.458 --> 00:03:01.375
Don't say that! That's brutally frank!

00:03:01.375 --> 00:03:02.958
--We've been working frantically

00:03:02.958 --> 00:03:04.958
--Miss, please don't get so excited!
--so they don't know about that!

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.792
Okay, having regained good
cheer, let's continue the show.

00:03:09.792 --> 00:03:11.958
Today's topic is the feature we
broadcast just a bit of before

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:14.333
and many people said that
they got hooked, oddly enough.

00:03:14.333 --> 00:03:16.667
"Pedro"

00:03:16.833 --> 00:03:17.667
--No! No!

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:19.250
<i>--The wandering soul,</i>
--No! No!

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.667
<i>Go, go, Pedro! In your own way!</i>

00:03:22.125 --> 00:03:22.958
"Pedro"

00:03:22.958 --> 00:03:23.833
<i>Pedro!</i>

00:03:23.833 --> 00:03:26.375
"Coming to Theaters Sometime"
<i>All you can do now is to watch over him!</i>

00:03:26.375 --> 00:03:28.417
"Coming to Theaters Sometime ...Maybe"

00:03:28.417 --> 00:03:32.667
Man, I can't believe they can
make this without getting complaints.

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:35.167
So, today's plan is to
take a persistent look back

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:37.375
at those days
that made such an impact!

00:03:37.375 --> 00:03:39.167
We're going back to
those slightly salty, pungent days

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:40.542
that we can never go back to. By force!

00:03:40.542 --> 00:03:42.333
Who cares about time paradoxes?!
Ignore them!

00:03:42.333 --> 00:03:43.667
Sadako probably
won't come out of the video!

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:45.000
I said we're gonna
look back, and that's that!

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:45.333
--It's decided! In other words...

00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:47.875
--In other words, they ran out of ideas.
--It's decided! In other words...

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.458
So what?! What's wrong with that?!

00:03:53.458 --> 00:03:55.458
We can't go back! It's not my fault!

00:03:55.458 --> 00:03:57.208
Mister, play the tape!

00:03:57.208 --> 00:03:58.792
Sure thing.

00:03:59.208 --> 00:04:01.083
"Mr. Pe"

00:04:02.042 --> 00:04:04.042
Pedro, you idiot!

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:10.875
--M-Miss Excel...

00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:12.917
--One more, you idiot!
--M-Miss Excel...

00:04:12.917 --> 00:04:15.542
Isn't that a little harsh?

00:04:15.542 --> 00:04:17.708
What are you going to
do by being weak like that?!

00:04:17.708 --> 00:04:20.917
If your son is really dear to
you and your wife is really sexy,

00:04:20.917 --> 00:04:23.375
then you should work
and sweat for the two of them!

00:04:23.375 --> 00:04:24.542
That's what's called true love!

00:04:24.542 --> 00:04:26.708
Pedro is shocked!

00:04:26.708 --> 00:04:29.542
T-True... love...

00:04:29.542 --> 00:04:34.208
That's right. Let's keep our
little complaints to ourselves.

00:04:34.208 --> 00:04:37.208
And right now, let's work!

00:04:37.208 --> 00:04:39.583
That is the path
that we part-timers walk!

00:04:39.583 --> 00:04:44.417
M-Miss Excel, my tears
are flowing like waterfalls!

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.875
Let's go, Pedro!

00:04:45.875 --> 00:04:47.583
Yes, Miss Excel!

00:04:48.375 --> 00:04:49.292
--Billy Jean!

00:04:49.292 --> 00:04:50.958
--John Travo...
--Billy Jean!

00:04:55.375 --> 00:04:56.958
That's right, this was how I, Excel,

00:04:56.958 --> 00:04:58.792
met the immigrant worker,
Pedro Domingo.

00:04:58.792 --> 00:05:00.292
Or rather,
we were already acquaintances.

00:05:00.292 --> 00:05:01.833
It seems they just
decided on his full name.

00:05:01.833 --> 00:05:04.500
The reason Pedro and I are
such good friends is...

00:05:07.292 --> 00:05:08.792
Some hypothesize that it's because

00:05:08.792 --> 00:05:10.917
both he and I don't fit into society at all.

00:05:10.917 --> 00:05:12.708
But I positively
dismiss it and strike it out.

00:05:12.708 --> 00:05:14.958
I... I...

00:05:14.958 --> 00:05:16.583
--I'm not playing this character

00:05:16.583 --> 00:05:18.250
--Senior has broken down.
--because I want to either!

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:18.875
--I've got my dreams too!

00:05:18.875 --> 00:05:19.958
--I'm sorry, would you  put the next one in now?
--I've got my dreams too!

00:05:19.958 --> 00:05:21.042
--I'm sorry, would you  put the next one in now?
--Scatter flowers like a maiden and go boom!

00:05:21.042 --> 00:05:22.792
--Sure thing.
--Scatter flowers like a maiden and go boom!

00:05:23.125 --> 00:05:25.042
"Pedro Dies at Dawn"

00:05:30.208 --> 00:05:31.625
Sandora!

00:05:38.625 --> 00:05:40.000
Pedro!

00:05:41.458 --> 00:05:42.167
--This is where it gets really awesome.

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:43.625
--It's hot! It's hot!
--This is where it gets really awesome.

00:05:43.625 --> 00:05:45.083
So, this is awesome?

00:05:45.083 --> 00:05:46.958
"No Reset"

00:05:49.542 --> 00:05:51.667
Poor Mr. Pedro.

00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:55.417
I will send you back to
your dear son and your sexy wife.

00:05:55.417 --> 00:05:59.917
Oh, it's time. I have to go. Ciao!

00:05:59.917 --> 00:06:02.625
No!

00:06:02.667 --> 00:06:04.583
"The Warmhearted Lady"

00:06:04.667 --> 00:06:06.875
Hot! It's hot!

00:06:10.792 --> 00:06:16.542
This is the room that
I shared with my coworkers.

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:20.458
Then, when I was covered
with flames last time...

00:06:20.458 --> 00:06:22.333
That was all a dream!

00:06:24.375 --> 00:06:26.167
Oh, Mr. Pe.

00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:30.167
No!

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:31.333
What did you think, Hatchan?

00:06:31.333 --> 00:06:34.333
The various truths that were
going on before you appeared...

00:06:34.333 --> 00:06:36.250
Situation after situation
that are so stupid, idiotic,

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.500
and needing apology that
it's hard to believe it's reality!

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:39.583
A waste, a waste, a waste, a waste!

00:06:39.583 --> 00:06:41.000
An entire waste of
both time and resources!

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.917
A drama worth less
than the simply ignored graffiti

00:06:42.917 --> 00:06:45.792
on the walls of public bathrooms
that display incredible sketching ability

00:06:45.792 --> 00:06:48.000
that never transcends the
hybrid and ecological aesthetics!

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.167
You can only be flabbergasted by it,
so let's be flabbergasted!

00:06:50.167 --> 00:06:51.000
--Senior?

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.000
--What?!
--Senior?

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.375
Don't ask who the hell the
Great Will of the Macrocosm is!

00:06:54.375 --> 00:06:56.708
And same as above
for what happened to Pedro!

00:06:57.708 --> 00:06:58.500
--I...

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.375
--Mister, without delay, next!
--I...

00:07:00.375 --> 00:07:02.042
Sure thing.

00:07:02.042 --> 00:07:03.917
"My Dear Home"

00:07:05.042 --> 00:07:06.875
Sandora!

00:07:06.875 --> 00:07:08.583
Welcome home!

00:07:08.583 --> 00:07:09.792
I'm home...

00:07:09.792 --> 00:07:12.375
Oh, you.

00:07:12.375 --> 00:07:13.875
Dear!

00:07:13.875 --> 00:07:15.625
W-Why?!

00:07:15.625 --> 00:07:19.458
Papa's home, so let's have dinner.

00:07:19.458 --> 00:07:20.375
Yeah!

00:07:20.375 --> 00:07:21.708
Papa?

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:26.458
Oh, Dear, he's become
completely attached to you.

00:07:27.458 --> 00:07:29.667
Well, he's not the only one, right?

00:07:29.667 --> 00:07:31.417
Oh, Dear!

00:07:34.583 --> 00:07:36.542
"Gomez"

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:44.125
T-They have me... But my son
and my sexy wife are with Gomez...

00:07:44.125 --> 00:07:46.583
No!

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.875
"Numbers That Don't Add Up"

00:07:50.708 --> 00:07:51.542
--What's wrong?!

00:07:51.542 --> 00:07:52.500
--Mama!
--What's wrong?!

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.458
You aren't...

00:07:54.458 --> 00:07:56.250
It looks like it.

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:58.750
Be happy, Sandora,
you'll have a kid brother!

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:00.292
Yay! All right!

00:08:00.292 --> 00:08:03.125
Why?! The numbers don't add up!

00:08:03.125 --> 00:08:05.917
Even when she was with me,
my wife and Gomez were...

00:08:05.917 --> 00:08:08.625
No!

00:08:10.792 --> 00:08:11.792
--Senior, you should not push it...

00:08:11.792 --> 00:08:13.083
--Never mind, next!
--Senior, you should not push it...

00:08:13.083 --> 00:08:13.542
Sure thing.

00:08:13.542 --> 00:08:15.458
"Why Are You There?"

00:08:16.125 --> 00:08:18.250
Can you see me?!

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:21.458
There's something I want
you to tell my wife and son!

00:08:23.458 --> 00:08:26.958
No! He does not understand me!

00:08:26.958 --> 00:08:28.833
"Reunion, O Wife"

00:08:29.167 --> 00:08:31.792
Welcome home, Dear!

00:08:31.792 --> 00:08:34.083
My darling Gomez!

00:08:34.083 --> 00:08:38.292
Wait a minute. I've brought
a guest with me today.

00:08:38.292 --> 00:08:39.333
Who?

00:08:39.333 --> 00:08:41.625
He says that he's a channeler.

00:08:41.625 --> 00:08:47.792
It's me! Your husband, Pedro!

00:08:47.792 --> 00:08:50.333
Shock!

00:08:50.375 --> 00:08:52.292
"Bogged Down"

00:08:52.542 --> 00:08:54.542
Shock? Come on, Dear.

00:08:54.542 --> 00:08:59.833
I came all this way by using
the body of a channeler to see you.

00:08:59.833 --> 00:09:03.833
--Shock. Shock. Shock. Shock.
--I don't think that's very fair of you.

00:09:03.833 --> 00:09:06.833
That's a lie! A lie, a lie!
Pedro kicked the bucket!

00:09:06.833 --> 00:09:09.375
But I <i>am </i>Pedro!

00:09:09.375 --> 00:09:12.625
It doesn't matter! Pedro
doesn't exist in my heart anymore!

00:09:12.625 --> 00:09:13.917
Not even a trace!

00:09:13.917 --> 00:09:17.292
Double shock!
And twin waterfalls of tears!

00:09:17.292 --> 00:09:19.667
A kick of reformation!

00:09:22.958 --> 00:09:26.583
I didn't want to do this.
I didn't, but...

00:09:26.583 --> 00:09:28.667
It was a good kick, Dear.

00:09:28.667 --> 00:09:31.083
Come, I'll comfort you.

00:09:31.083 --> 00:09:33.750
Dear, it's the middle of the day.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:37.875
I have lost my physical body
and I have lost the love of my wife.

00:09:37.875 --> 00:09:41.542
Can there possibly be anyone
who could understand my sorrow?

00:09:41.542 --> 00:09:43.083
I want to shout out!

00:09:43.083 --> 00:09:45.875
From the bottom of my
heart and with all my might,

00:09:45.875 --> 00:09:48.083
very <i>no</i>!

00:09:50.542 --> 00:09:52.250
What a story that gets to your eyes!

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:53.875
True and loving Lord Ilpalazzo,

00:09:53.875 --> 00:09:55.667
for whom I feel endless love
and respect and serve devotedly!

00:09:55.667 --> 00:09:57.250
I had no idea such events
were happening over and over

00:09:57.250 --> 00:09:59.042
while I was on city conquest
missions that I push myself

00:09:59.042 --> 00:10:00.750
to go on purely because I want
to see your smile!

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:02.208
Piteous! Just so piteous!

00:10:02.208 --> 00:10:03.708
Do these tears flow
from my eyes like waterfalls

00:10:03.708 --> 00:10:05.250
because I'm an anime?!
Or because I'm human?!

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.542
In any case, isn't this treatment
of a mere immigrant worker,

00:10:07.542 --> 00:10:09.958
who does not even appear
in the original work, far too cruel?!

00:10:09.958 --> 00:10:12.542
Was the creator somehow
traumatized in the past?!

00:10:12.542 --> 00:10:14.583
Or was it just harassment?!
Tell me straight! Come out!

00:10:14.583 --> 00:10:15.625
'Ello.

00:10:15.625 --> 00:10:16.708
Mister, give me my usual.

00:10:16.708 --> 00:10:17.750
Sure thing.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:20.083
Well, hello, Mr. Director.
I hope everything is going well.

00:10:20.083 --> 00:10:22.083
Here's your usual!

00:10:22.083 --> 00:10:25.125
This is it! This, right before
the commercials, is still the best!

00:10:25.125 --> 00:10:27.125
Rubbing, rubbing egg white on.

00:10:29.042 --> 00:10:31.458
The yolk is all mushy!

00:10:31.458 --> 00:10:33.458
I don't want that kind of fried eggs...

00:10:33.458 --> 00:10:35.375
"Love at Ghost Bar"

00:10:36.583 --> 00:10:38.708
Sandora and wife...

00:10:38.708 --> 00:10:41.083
I'll never again see love in
this world.

00:10:41.083 --> 00:10:43.042
There, make that one your last.

00:10:43.042 --> 00:10:44.792
Don't mind me.

00:10:46.375 --> 00:10:47.958
Ms. Will!

00:10:47.958 --> 00:10:51.958
You can pick up love off the
ground anywhere. Even here.

00:10:54.542 --> 00:10:56.417
Ms. Will!

00:10:56.417 --> 00:11:00.125
Oh, you're so hopeless without me.

00:11:00.625 --> 00:11:02.500
"His Name Is 'That Man'"

00:11:03.792 --> 00:11:05.625
Ms. Will...

00:11:07.167 --> 00:11:08.750
Open up, damn you!

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:09.750
Who is it?

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:11.917
I know you're in there, you bitch!

00:11:11.917 --> 00:11:13.792
Oh, no! It's That Man!

00:11:13.792 --> 00:11:15.125
That man?

00:11:15.125 --> 00:11:16.833
I'm coming in!

00:11:16.833 --> 00:11:19.708
No! I didn't do it!

00:11:19.708 --> 00:11:21.083
I shall explain!

00:11:21.083 --> 00:11:23.292
This dangerous-seeming, real
scary man, who suddenly appeared

00:11:23.292 --> 00:11:25.500
and seems to be related somehow
to the Great Will of the Macrocosm,

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:27.958
is commonly known as "That Man".
It said so in the script too.

00:11:27.958 --> 00:11:29.875
We thought he was a side
character and didn't give him a name,

00:11:29.875 --> 00:11:32.125
but before we knew it,
even as we said no, no, no,

00:11:32.125 --> 00:11:33.958
he became a fixed regular.
Was that because his face

00:11:33.958 --> 00:11:35.542
was like Kawaguchi or Noujou?

00:11:35.542 --> 00:11:37.000
But no matter how mistaken you were,

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.667
it's definitely not Fukumoto.
Right, Hatchan?

00:11:43.833 --> 00:11:46.833
Why do you die so easily?!
Don't you have any intention of living?!

00:11:46.833 --> 00:11:48.750
"But I'm A Ghost"

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:51.083
P-Please calm down!

00:11:51.083 --> 00:11:53.917
You took my woman! How dare you
tell me to calm down?!

00:11:53.917 --> 00:11:55.625
S-So, I'm saying...

00:11:55.625 --> 00:11:57.625
That's "I'm sorry," right?! Hey?!

00:11:58.625 --> 00:12:00.500
"I Didn't Know Anything"

00:12:01.583 --> 00:12:03.583
May I say something?

00:12:04.333 --> 00:12:09.000
Since I laid my hands on
Ms. Will, where are you taking me?

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:10.250
Tokyo Bay.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:13.250
No!

00:12:16.542 --> 00:12:19.542
What will Pedro's fate be?

00:12:19.542 --> 00:12:23.833
H-He's a ghost,
so how can he ride in the car?

00:12:23.833 --> 00:12:25.417
For the sake of the production staff,

00:12:25.417 --> 00:12:27.042
don't ask things like that.

00:12:27.042 --> 00:12:28.875
